WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.667
-Our next guest is the cohost of the podcast

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:05.300
"In the Minivan" with Max and Mike,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.934
available on Spotify.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.400
Making his late-night debut,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.400
please welcome the very funny Michael Rowland.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:18.467
♪♪

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.234
-Thank you.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:23.067
Thank you, thank you. Appreciate it, everybody.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.133
I was talking to my buddy the other day,

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.400
and I asked him how he spends his free time.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.968
He told me every day he likes to go to the park and people-watch.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:34.234
Why is that okay? People-watch.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.200
Just 'cause we flip the words around it's not creepy anymore?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.601
[ Laughter ] You know?

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.067
Because it'd be much different if her was like,

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:45.234
"Yeah, every day I go to the park...and watch people."

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:47.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.868
But we just flip the words,

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.901
and now it's like this cultured pastime.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.334
He's like, "Yeah, go to the park and people-watch.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.367
Sometimes I people-follow."

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:05.200
"And, you know, if I really like 'em, I'll people-touch."

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.934
Uh...

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.033
A cultured guy.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.234
I'm from the South originally.

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:12.834
We all know the South can be a little bit backwards,

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.334
behind the times.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.634
For instance, did you know that they just legalized doing yoga

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.868
in schools in Alabama?

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.601
I'm sorry. Did you know it was illegal

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.834
to do yoga in schools in Alabama?

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:25.000
It was illegal for 30 years.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.934
And they just legalized it last year.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.234
But, if you're doing it,

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.634
you can't use any of the classic yoga terminology,

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:31.734
none of the Sanskrit words,

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.801
because they consider it Eastern religion.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.033
So you can do the poses, but you can't say the words.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.400
Which is insane. I don't even know how you do that.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.167
I feel like yoga in Alabama is just like, "Alright.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.767
We're gonna do a Dukes of Hazzard

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.734
into a Jimmy Buffett."

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:50.400
"And we're gonna finish up bringing hands to heart center.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.067
Altogether now. Roll Tide. Unh."

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:57.834
[ Applause ]

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.067
I'm from Atlanta myself, but I always wanted to live

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:06.667
here in New York ever since I was a kid.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.334
'Cause when I was a kid, I would spend the summers

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:10.367
in Savannah, Georgia, with my grandma.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:11.968
And we would just watch episodes

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:15.000
of "Sex and the City" back to back to back.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.267
Yeah, and I would fantasize about moving to New York

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.033
and being a little slut.

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:22.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.000
That's right.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.567
Yeah.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:29.634
And my grandma was like, "Oh, you can do it, baby.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:33.334
Yeah. You get up there. You're Grandma's Carrie."

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:34.801
That's how my grandma is.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.167
My grandma's, like, this fun, vivacious Southern woman.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:38.367
She says wild stuff.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.167
I remember once I was talking to my grandma.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:41.934
And I was like, "Grandma, what was it like

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.033
being a young lady growing up in Georgia?"

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.300
And my grandma's response, word for word, she goes,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.133
"Michael, when I was 18, all the boys came back

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.734
from World War II, and we had a good time."

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:56.667
Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.767
It was a very specific answer to a very broad question.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.567
Do you notice how broad?

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.334
It's interesting 'cause she's a very fun lady.

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.734
She gave birth to my mom.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:06.634
My mom's much more "type A" and neurotic.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:08.434
And I worried her a lot when I was kid

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.934
'cause I have severe nut allergies.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.968
And when I was growing up, she was so worried I was

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.968
going to eat something with nuts in it, she went over the top.

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.234
It was embarrassing.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.033
I remember she made this big poster that was like,

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:22.234
"Warning! Michael Rowland is allergic to nuts!"

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.968
And she took that poster and she hung it on the wall

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.734
in my middle-school nurse's office.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:29.334
So kids would come back from the nurse's office and be like,

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:32.167
"Yo, I saw your poster."

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.934
Kids always said the same thing.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.334
They'd be like, "Mike, you allergic to nuts.

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:38.534
You allergic to deez nuts?"

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:39.968
Every time.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.834
And I wasn't like a clever kid,

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:45.167
so I'd just be like, "Yeah, uh, I'm allergic to doze."

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.234
I was also very undersized when I was kid.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:51.334
Like, when I started high school, I was 4'11."

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:54.567
It's true. I was 14 years old. I was 4'11."

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.334
And my mom -- You know how she is.

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:59.133
She was like, "We've got to go to a doctor right now!"

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:00.601
So I remember she took me to see

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.634
this specialist called an endocrinologist.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.734
And this endocrinologist examined

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:06.667
my little 4'11" skeleton.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.868
And he came to me and he was like, "Yes.

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:13.334
You have the bones of a person two years younger than you."

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:18.033
And I remember. I was just like, "Yo, um, are they my bones?

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.901
Like...

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:23.200
who has my bones right now?"

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.868
He never explained it to me.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:27.434
So I just like to imagine that I was an experiment

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.367
in the same lab that made Wolverine

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:30.767
and changed his skeleton out.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.200
'Cause you know Wolverine, the X-Men,

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.934
they changed out his skeleton in that lab.

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:35.367
That's the skeleton-changing lab.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:36.834
And that lab is full of scientists.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.567
And those scientists are going to experiment,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.767
and they're not all going to be winners, you know?

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:43.400
So I like to imagine one scientist like,

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.167
"Yes, this is Wolverine.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.834
We gave him unbreakable bones of adamantium.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.234
And this is Mike.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:52.701
We gave him the bones of a slightly younger boy."

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:55.901
Yes.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.834
[ Applause ]

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.701
Thank you.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.200
My body did eventually grow,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.033
and I moved here to New York City where I live now.

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.000
But I went back to Georgia recently to visit my grandma.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.501
That was great.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:12.167
She just got a new flat-screen TV at the house, which is nice.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.067
She lost the remote, though. Which --

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:16.801
Have you ever tried to turn on a new flat-screen TV

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:18.367
without the remote?

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:21.567
You will never feel dumber in your whole life.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.534
All you want to do is watch TV,

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:26.200
but you're just stuck there like...

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.701
[ Applause ]

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:49.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.234
I mean, it's so hard, you might as well go to the park

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:57.534
and watch people. You know what I mean?

00:05:57.534 --> 00:06:00.067
Alright. Thank you. Thank you.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:02.267
♪♪

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:05.868
-Oh, my gosh. That was a perfect set.

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:07.400
That was unbelievable.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.567
That's how you do it right there. Michael Rowland.

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:13.267
[ Cheers and applause ] That was a perfect set.

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.067
"In the Minivan" with Max and Mike

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:18.300
is available on Spotify. We'll be right back, everybody.

